# Writing your own functional interface

## The recipe — one abstract method + `@FunctionalInterface`

```java
@FunctionalInterface
public interface DiscountRule {
    BigDecimal apply(Order order);      // the single abstract method
}

DiscountRule loyalty = order -> order.total().multiply(new BigDecimal("0.9"));
```

The annotation makes the compiler **enforce** the SAM rule.

## `default` / `static` are fine — only *abstract* methods count

```java
default DiscountRule andCap(BigDecimal max) {
    return order -> apply(order).min(max);
}
```

## When to write one

- **Domain clarity** — `DiscountRule` beats a bare `Function<Order, BigDecimal>`
- **A shape built-ins lack** — 3 inputs, odd arity
- **Checked exceptions** — `T get() throws IOException`

**Otherwise: use the standard interface.** Don't re-say `Function`/`Predicate`.
